+/// differences are quantization noise rather than slope, so a straight secant crawls a tick at a
+/// time. With the vertex value `d_v` at `v` and one probe `(t, d)`, `d(s) = d_v + B·(v − s)²`
+/// puts the level at `v − (v − t)·sqrt(−d_v/(d − d_v))`: the square-root scaling a flat branch
+/// asks for. `None` on any degeneracy (the secant or the midpoint then places the probe).
+fn flat_branch(v: i64, d_v: f64, t: i64, d: f64) -> Option<i64> {
+    let x = (v - t) as f64 * (-d_v / (d - d_v)).sqrt();
+    (x.is_finite() && x >= 1.0).then(|| v - x as i64)
+}
